Updated Detailed Explanation of Gym Membership Pause/Resume System with Gym Access Control
System Overview
The gym membership pause/resume system allows members with specific package types to temporarily pause their memberships while preserving their remaining time. When they resume, their membership end date is extended by the number of days they were paused. Additionally, the system now controls physical gym access by blocking/unblocking their entry cards.

Core Concepts
1. Two-Tier Package System
The gym has 23 eligible packages divided into two tiers:

Tier 1 (Premium Packages): 10 packages offering 60 days of pause allowance

These are typically longer-term or more expensive memberships
Examples: Package 1317 (1-year membership), Package 1237, etc.
Tier 2 (Standard Packages): 13 packages offering 30 days of pause allowance

These are typically shorter-term or standard memberships
Examples: Package 1365, Package 1205, etc.
2. Dual Control System
The pause system now controls two separate aspects:

A) Membership Status (SoldPackages table):

Tracks pause dates and remaining days
Manages membership extensions
B) Physical Gym Access (clientcards table):

Controls whether member can enter gym premises
Managed through activeindevice field
3. Package Eligibility Rules
Not all gym packages can be paused. Only the 23 pre-defined packages are eligible. When a member tries to pause:

✅ Eligible: Member has Package 1365 → Can pause (30-day allowance) ❌ Not Eligible: Member has Package 1111 → Cannot pause (not in eligible list)

4. Active Package Detection
The system only considers packages that are currently active:

Package must not be manually expired (Expired = 0)
Package end date must be in the future (EndDate > today)
If a member has multiple packages, only the active one counts
