Business Logic Flow with Access Control
When Member Loads Profile Page
Package Check: What packages does this member have?
Eligibility Filter: Only non-expired, future-dated packages from eligible list
Tier Determination: 30-day or 60-day allowance based on package
Status Display: Current pause status and remaining days
Access Status: Not displayed but controlled in background
When Member Clicks "Pause Membership"
Validation Phase:

Confirms member has eligible, active package
Ensures not already paused
Confirms remaining pause days > 0
Database Updates (Two-Table Operation):

SoldPackages Table:

PauseStatus = 1
PauseStartDate = current date
Remainingpause = package maximum (if first time)
clientcards Table:

activeindevice = false (blocks gym access)
Immediate Effects:

Profile shows paused status
Gym card immediately deactivated
Confirmation message sent
When Member Clicks "Resume Membership"
Calculation Phase:

Finds currently paused membership
Calculates total days paused
Deducts paused days from remaining allowance
Calculates new membership end date
Database Updates (Two-Table Operation):

SoldPackages Table:

PauseStatus = 0
PauseEndDate = current date
Remainingpause = updated amount
EndDate = extended by paused days
clientcards Table:

activeindevice = true (restores gym access)
Immediate Effects:

Profile shows active status
Gym card immediately reactivated
New end date displayed
Physical Gym Access Integration
Entry System Behavior:

When activeindevice = true:

Card scan → Green light → Gate opens
Normal gym access granted
When activeindevice = false (during pause):

Card scan → Red light → Gate remains closed
Display shows "Access Denied" or similar message
Member cannot enter gym premises
Edge Cases and Protections with Access Control
Case 1: Package Expires During Pause
Membership end date still gets extended when resumed
Gym access remains blocked until resume is clicked
Member gets back all their lost time
Case 2: Zero Days Remaining
Pause button becomes permanently disabled (0/30 or 0/60)
Gym access remains enabled (no automatic blocking)
Member keeps their remaining membership time
Case 3: System Failures
If clientcards update fails during pause: Member can still enter gym (fail-safe)
If clientcards update fails during resume: Member may need manual intervention
Error logging captures these issues for manual review
Case 4: Member Switches Packages
If member buys new package while paused, system uses new package's tier
Gym access control remains based on pause status regardless of package
Case 5: Database Inconsistencies
If SoldPackages shows paused but clientcards shows active: Member can enter gym
If SoldPackages shows active but clientcards shows blocked: Member cannot enter gym
Admin tools needed to resolve such inconsistencies
